		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=1212&amp;p=10749#p10749"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div>Hi all.<br><br>Just thought i would share my issues with the GD77 not powering on.<br>Unit had something rattling around in it and radio would not power on.<br><br>After removing the main-board I found a small bit of solder floating around in the unit, this caused the issues.  <br>Note - removing the GD77 main-board requires de-soldering the antenna connection, see attached picture.<br><br>I then discovered a little fuse on the board that had blown, (Littelfuse 3A FF Surface Mount Fuse, 32V ac/dc) <br><a href="https://au.rs-online.com/web/p/non-resettable-surface-mount-fuses/5413619/" class="postlink">https://au.rs-online.com/web/p/non-rese ... s/5413619/</a><br><br>Replaced the fuse and the unit works again, hopefully this helps someone that has a non working unit.<br><br>De-solder the antenna connection image.<br><a href="https://ibb.co/J37wbHB" class="postlink">https://ibb.co/J37wbHB</a><br><br>Fuse location Image <br><a href="https://ibb.co/GtStD2j" class="postlink">https://ibb.co/GtStD2j</a></div></blockquote>Very useful.<br><br>Thankyou<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Thu Sep 03, 2020 9:50 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
